Yani for new item: Top Hat

Can be worn but has zero armour rating (unless enchanted). Any wizard,
necromancer or mage (a)pplying a top hat will produce a rabbit at a
cost of- let's say- 8 magic power points.

Any non-spellcaster (a)pplying a top hat will produce a rabbit 20% of
the time at a cost of 20 magic power points, or will get "nothing
happens" 80% of the time at a cost of 1 mgaic point.

Gnomish wizards/ orc shamans and the like should pick up top hats and
use them to generate rabbits. NPC generated rabbits are always
hostile. To avoid abuse though (ie, lock a gnomish wizard in a temple
with a top hat to generate dozens of sacrificial bunnies) NPCs should
only use a top hat if there are less than three rabbits on the level
already.

(a)pplying a hat- whether successful or not- takes two turns.

If a player chooses to wear a top hat, every now and again (1/1000
chance every turn the hat is worn) it will spit out a rabbit anyway,
at no power cost to the wearer. Hostile rabbits produced this way get
a free "surprise" attack on the wearer of the hat.

Rabbits generated while a player character is holding/wearing the hat
have a 10% chance of being tame, all others are hostile. This makes it
a little harder to generate rabbits for food/ sacrifice at will.

Enchanted hats produce proportionally tougher/ weaker animals. (ie a
+4 hat produces a really hard rabbit.)

A top hat has an infinite number of charges. (The cost is in magic
power, not charges.)

If a top hat is burnt/corroded/damaged, substitute the word "rat" for
"rabbit" in all the above text.

This would work best in Slashem which already includes rabbits as
monsters, but anyone willing/able to patch a top hat into vanilla
could also put in a rabbit.

